# ── Never publish ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The AI Automation project is SEPARATE and lives in its own repo
# (vengateshb12/zcat-design-system). What sits here is a link to a folder on
# one specific Mac — committing it would give every user a broken pointer.
# Its rules reach consumers through the zcat MCP instead:
#   https://zcat.catalystappsail.in/mcp
/AI Automation
/AI Automation alias

# Internal session notes: Figma file keys, account details, library debt,
# designer-review status. Not for consumers of the library.
HANDOFF.md

# Pages built with the library — the author's own work, not part of it.
# Pages you build are yours and stay out of the repo — EXCEPT the handful the
# docs depend on. build-snippets.py extracts real component markup from these,
# so if they are ignored a fresh clone regenerates snippets.html with one source
# instead of six and most components vanish, silently. They are reference
# material, not page-build output.
/pages/*
!/pages/directdb/
!/pages/samples/

# STALE DOCS — kept locally, never published. Both describe markup that no
# longer exists, and COMPONENTS.md is the file a new developer opens first by
# convention, so shipping it would start every consumer from wrong information.
# The live contract is zcat-ui/ONBOARDING.md.
zcat-ui/COMPONENTS.md
zcat-ui/docs/index.html

# ── Machine / build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# Hook working state: screenshots, audit receipts and review records are
# regenerated locally on every run and are specific to one machine.
.claude/hooks/.zcat-state/
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Deploy artefact — regenerated by build-docs-site.sh on every deploy.
/slate-docs

# Deploy config: carries the Catalyst project id and an absolute path from one
# machine, so it is useless (and leaky) in a public clone.
catalyst.json
.zcat-unlock
